WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:35.002
<b><i>Sub by: ChesterJohn</i>.</b>

2
00:00:51.799 --> 00:00:53.289
<i>"Do you ever look
at someone and wonder...</i>

3
00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.648
<i>"What is going on
inside their head?"</i>

4
00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:59.402
<i>Well, I know.
Well, I know Riley's head.</i>

5
00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:36.640
Hmm?

6
00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.602
<i>And there she was...</i>

7
00:01:48.359 --> 00:01:52.081
Hello. Riley.

8
00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:54.204
Oh, look at you.

9
00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:56.524
Aren't you a
little bundle of joy?

10
00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.763
<i>Aren't you a little
bundle of joy?</i>

11
00:02:10.719 --> 00:02:11.960
Whoa.

12
00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:34.723
<i>It was amazing.
Just Riley and me. Forever.</i>

13
00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.481
Err, for 33 seconds?

14
00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:47.409
I'm Sadness.

15
00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:50.848
Oh, hello.
I... I'm Joy. So...

16
00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:53.125
Can I just... If you could...

17
00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:54.764
I just want to fix that. Thanks.

18
00:02:55.439 --> 00:02:57.090
<i>And that was
just the beginning.</i>

19
00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:59.486
<i>Headquarters only got
more crowded from there.</i>

20
00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:05.060
Very nice. Okay, looks like
you got this. Very good.

21
00:03:05.159 --> 00:03:06.764
Whoa, sharp turn!
No! Look out! No!

22
00:03:06.879 --> 00:03:07.879
<i>That's Fear.</i>

23
00:03:07.919 --> 00:03:10.048
<i>He's really good
at keeping Riley safe.</i>

24
00:03:10.599 --> 00:03:11.900
Easy, easy. Ah!

25
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.889
Oh,
we're good. We're good.

26
00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:16.485
- Whew! Good job.
- Thank you. Thank you very much.

27
00:03:16.599 --> 00:03:18.020
And we're back!

28
00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:20.122
Oh!

29
00:03:22.719 --> 00:03:24.085
Here we go. All right, open.

30
00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:25.963
- Hmm. This looks new.
- You think it's safe?

31
00:03:26.079 --> 00:03:27.205
- What is it?
- Aah.

32
00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:30.060
Okay, caution.
There is a dangerous smell, people.

33
00:03:30.159 --> 00:03:32.219
- Hold on. What is that?
<i>- This is Disgust.</i>

34
00:03:32.319 --> 00:03:34.800
<i>She basically keeps Riley
from being poisoned.</i>

35
00:03:35.039 --> 00:03:36.200
<i>Physically and socially.</i>

36
00:03:36.319 --> 00:03:37.620
<i>That is not brightly colored</i>

37
00:03:37.719 --> 00:03:39.324
<i>or shaped like a dinosaur.
Hold on, guys.</i>

38
00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:40.780
It's broccoli!

39
00:03:40.879 --> 00:03:41.881
Yucky!

40
00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:45.259
Well, I just saved our lives.

41
00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:46.539
- Whew!
- Yeah. You're welcome.

42
00:03:46.639 --> 00:03:48.079
Riley, if you don't eat your dinner,

43
00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:49.460
you're not gonna get any dessert.

44
00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:51.881
Wait. Did he just say
we couldn't have dessert?

45
00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.099
<i>That's Anger.</i>

46
00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:56.300
<i>He cares very deeply
about things being fair.</i>

47
00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.219
So that's how you
want to play it, old man?

48
00:03:58.319 --> 00:04:01.289
No dessert? Oh, sure,
we'll eat our dinner!

49
00:04:01.479 --> 00:04:03.419
Right after you eat this!

50
00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:09.259
Riley, Riley,
here comes an airplane!

51
00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:13.206
Oh, airplane.
We got an airplane, everybody.

52
00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:14.480
- Oh!
- Airplane.

53
00:04:23.439 --> 00:04:26.728
<i>And you've met Sadness.
She... Well, she...</i>

54
00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:32.889
<i>I'm not actually sure
what she does.</i>

55
00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:34.245
<i>And I've checked,</i>

56
00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:35.620
<i>there's no place for her to go, so...</i>

57
00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:38.199
<i>She's good,
we're good. It's all great!</i>

58
00:04:38.879 --> 00:04:40.779
<i>Anyway, these are Riley's memories</i>

59
00:04:40.879 --> 00:04:42.959
<i>and they're mostly happy,
you'll notice. Not to brag.</i>

60
00:04:43.079 --> 00:04:44.605
Whoo-hoo!

61
00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:47.000
Whoo-hoo!

62
00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.643
<i>But the really
important ones are over here.</i>

63
00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:52.480
<i>I don't want to get too technical,</i>

64
00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:54.641
<i>but these are called Core Memories.</i>

65
00:04:55.079 --> 00:04:58.209
<i>Each one came from
a super important time in Riley's life.</i>

66
00:04:58.399 --> 00:05:00.050
<i>Uh, like when she first scored a goal.</i>

67
00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:01.571
<i>Oh, that was so amazing!</i>

68
00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:04.290
Hey! Would you look at that? Very nice!

69
00:05:04.399 --> 00:05:05.660
- We got a future center here!
- Nice job.

70
00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:19.766
<i>And each Core Memory</i>

71
00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:22.446
<i>powers a different aspect
of Riley's personality.</i>

72
00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:24.809
<i>Like Hockey Island.</i>

73
00:05:27.199 --> 00:05:29.281
<i>Goofball Island
is my personal favorite.</i>

74
00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.802
Ah, come back here,
you little monkey!

75
00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.860
Oh, you're silly.

76
00:05:34.959 --> 00:05:36.723
<i>Yep, Goofball is the best.</i>

77
00:05:37.159 --> 00:05:39.127
<i>Friendship Island
is pretty good too.</i>

78
00:05:41.879 --> 00:05:44.120
<i>Oh, I love Honesty Island.</i>

79
00:05:44.399 --> 00:05:45.401
<i>And that's the truth!</i>

80
00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:47.922
<i>And of course,
Family Island is amazing.</i>

81
00:05:50.399 --> 00:05:52.606
<i>The point is,
the Islands of Personality</i>

82
00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:54.768
<i>are what make Riley... Riley!</i>

83
00:05:55.079 --> 00:05:57.286
Look out, mermaid!

84
00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:04.610
Lava! Whee!

85
00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:08.259
<i>? Who's your friend who likes to play?</i>

86
00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:10.009
<i>? Bing Bong, Bing Bong! ?</i>

87
00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:12.444
- Hey! Very nice!
- Where'd you learn that?

88
00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:17.648
Ahhh!

89
00:06:17.759 --> 00:06:20.809
Brain freeze!

90
00:06:24.399 --> 00:06:26.528
Yeah!

91
00:06:30.079 --> 00:06:31.081
Good night, kiddo.

92
00:06:31.319 --> 00:06:32.367
Good night, Dad.

93
00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:40.324
And... we're out!

94
00:06:41.399 --> 00:06:42.620
That's what I'm talking about!

95
00:06:42.720 --> 00:06:44.165
Whoo! Another perfect day!

96
00:06:44.279 --> 00:06:45.420
Nice job, everybody!

97
00:06:45.519 --> 00:06:47.199
Let's get those memories
down to Long Term.

98
00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:54.129
All right, we did not die today!

99
00:06:54.279 --> 00:06:56.009
I call that an unqualified success.

100
00:07:11.959 --> 00:07:14.420
<i>And that's it. We love our girl.</i>

101
00:07:14.519 --> 00:07:16.442
<i>She's got great friends
and a great house.</i>

102
00:07:16.839 --> 00:07:18.204
<i>Things couldn't be better.</i>

103
00:07:18.879 --> 00:07:20.689
<i>After all, Riley's 11 now.</i>

104
00:07:21.519 --> 00:07:22.521
<i>What could happen?</i>

105
00:07:24.199 --> 00:07:25.281
- What...
- Aah!

106
00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:32.043
Okay, not what I had in mind.

107
00:07:56.879 --> 00:07:58.769
Hey, look!
The Golden Gate Bridge!

108
00:07:58.879 --> 00:07:59.927
Isn't that great?

109
00:08:00.079 --> 00:08:02.300
It's not made out of
solid gold like we thought,

110
00:08:02.399 --> 00:08:04.129
which is kind of
a disappointment, but still...

111
00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:06.766
I sure am glad you told me
earthquakes are a myth, Joy.

112
00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.139
Otherwise I'd be terrified right now!

113
00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:10.605
Uh, yeah...

114
00:08:10.959 --> 00:08:11.927
Are you kidding?
Get out of the street!

115
00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:13.279
Oh, for Pete's sake! Move it!

116
00:08:13.399 --> 00:08:15.401
These are my kind of people.

117
00:08:15.759 --> 00:08:17.285
All right,
just a few more blocks.

118
00:08:17.399 --> 00:08:18.660
We're almost to our new house!

119
00:08:18.759 --> 00:08:19.807
Step on it, Daddy!

120
00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:21.139
Why don't we just live
in this smelly car?

121
00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:22.651
We've already been in it forever.

122
00:08:22.759 --> 00:08:24.540
Which, actually, was really lucky,

123
00:08:24.639 --> 00:08:26.220
because that gave us
plenty of time to think about

124
00:08:26.319 --> 00:08:28.540
what our new house
is going to look like!

125
00:08:28.639 --> 00:08:30.846
What! Let's review
the top five daydreams.

126
00:08:31.439 --> 00:08:33.090
- Ooh! That looks safe!
- That one's nice.

127
00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:34.605
Oh, this will be great for Riley!

128
00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:35.926
Oh, no, no, no, no, this one!

129
00:08:36.039 --> 00:08:38.042
Oh, Joy, for the last time,
she cannot live in a cookie.

130
00:08:38.159 --> 00:08:40.128
That's the one!
It comes with a dragon.

131
00:08:41.759 --> 00:08:43.480
Now we're getting close,
I can feel it.

132
00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:46.763
Here it is, here's our new house.

133
00:08:47.279 --> 00:08:48.280
And...

134
00:08:54.440 --> 00:08:56.363
Maybe it's nice on the inside.

135
00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:03.860
- We're supposed to live here?
- Do we have to?

136
00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:05.899
I'm telling you,
it smells like something died in here.

137
00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:07.059
Can you die from moving?

138
00:09:07.159 --> 00:09:08.580
Guys, you're overreacting.

139
00:09:08.679 --> 00:09:10.010
Nobody is dying...

140
00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:11.139
A dead mouse!

141
00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:13.019
- Great. This is just great.
- I'm gonna be sick.

142
00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:14.539
It's the house of the dead!
We're going to get rabies!

143
00:09:14.639 --> 00:09:16.085
Get off of me!

144
00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:17.460
Hey. All through the drive,

145
00:09:17.559 --> 00:09:19.419
Dad talked about
how cool our new room is.

146
00:09:19.519 --> 00:09:20.567
Let's go check it out!

147
00:09:20.679 --> 00:09:21.700
- Let's go!
- It's gonna be great!

148
00:09:21.799 --> 00:09:22.801
Yes, yes, yes.

149
00:09:23.159 --> 00:09:24.159
No, no, no, no, no.

150
00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:25.460
I'm starting
to envy the dead mouse.

151
00:09:25.559 --> 00:09:26.539
Get out the rubber ball,

152
00:09:26.639 --> 00:09:27.940
we're in solitary confinement.

153
00:09:28.039 --> 00:09:29.039
Riley can't live here.

154
00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:30.100
- She's right.
- It's the worst.

155
00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:31.580
- Really bad.
- It's absolutely the worst.

156
00:09:31.679 --> 00:09:34.159
It's the worst place
I've ever been in my entire life.

157
00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:36.799
Hey, it's nothing
our butterfly curtains couldn't fix.

158
00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:39.162
I read somewhere
that an empty room is an opportunity.

159
00:09:39.279 --> 00:09:40.691
- Where did you read that?
- It doesn't matter.

160
00:09:40.799 --> 00:09:41.799
I read it and it's great.

161
00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:42.899
We'll put the bed there.

162
00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:44.059
And the desk over there.

163
00:09:44.159 --> 00:09:45.321
The hockey lamp goes there.

164
00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:46.402
Uh, put the chair there.

165
00:09:46.519 --> 00:09:48.039
The trophy collection goes there.

166
00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:49.659
Stars! I like that!

167
00:09:49.759 --> 00:09:50.841
Now we're talking!

168
00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:52.679
Let's go get our stuff
from the moving van!

169
00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:54.565
All right. Goodbye.

170
00:09:54.679 --> 00:09:55.679
Well, guess what?

171
00:09:55.759 --> 00:09:57.480
The moving van
won't be here until Thursday.

172
00:09:57.519 --> 00:09:58.940
- You're kidding.
- Mmm-hmm.

173
00:09:59.039 --> 00:10:01.299
The van is lost?
It is the worst day ever!

174
00:10:01.399 --> 00:10:02.960
That figures. The van is lost.

175
00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:04.500
You said it would be here yesterday!

176
00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:05.885
I know that's what I said.
That's what they told me!

177
00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.047
Mom and Dad are stressed out!

178
00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:08.969
- They're stressed out?
- What are we going to do?

179
00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:11.559
I've got a great idea!

180
00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:14.250
Did you even read the contract?

181
00:10:14.519 --> 00:10:16.860
Andersen makes her move.
She's closing in!

182
00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:17.960
Hey!

183
00:10:18.039 --> 00:10:19.041
Oh, no, you're not!

184
00:10:19.159 --> 00:10:20.179
She's lining up for the shot!

185
00:10:20.279 --> 00:10:21.279
Coming behind you.

186
00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:23.124
- Watch out! Watch out!
- She shoots and she scores!

187
00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:24.809
Yeah!

188
00:10:25.879 --> 00:10:27.961
- Come on, Grandma!
- Ha!

189
00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:29.200
"Grandma"?

190
00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:31.004
Uh-oh, she put her hair up,
we're in for it!

191
00:10:31.399 --> 00:10:32.605
Whoo!

192
00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:34.500
Hey, put me down!

193
00:10:37.879 --> 00:10:39.539
Ah! Sorry.

194
00:10:39.639 --> 00:10:40.687
Hold on. Hold on.

195
00:10:41.559 --> 00:10:43.562
- Hello?
- Wait. Wh...

196
00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:44.846
You're kidding.

197
00:10:45.759 --> 00:10:47.284
All right. Stall for me.

198
00:10:47.399 --> 00:10:48.400
I'll be right there.

199
00:10:48.879 --> 00:10:50.340
The investor's supposed
to show up on Thursday,

200
00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:51.600
not today!

201
00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:53.130
I got to go.

202
00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:54.605
It's okay. We get it.

203
00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:55.926
You're the best. Thanks, hon.

204
00:10:56.639 --> 00:10:57.879
See you, sweetie.

205
00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:00.299
Dad just left us.

206
00:11:00.399 --> 00:11:01.980
He doesn't love us anymore.

207
00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:03.240
That's sad.

208
00:11:03.399 --> 00:11:04.889
I should drive, right?

209
00:11:05.399 --> 00:11:06.447
Joy?

210
00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:08.285
What are you doing?

211
00:11:08.399 --> 00:11:09.970
Uh, just give me one second.

212
00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:12.089
Um, you know what I've realized?

213
00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:14.561
Riley hasn't had lunch! Remember?

214
00:11:17.159 --> 00:11:19.580
Hey, I saw a pizza place
down the street.

215
00:11:19.679 --> 00:11:20.740
Maybe we could try that?

216
00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:22.179
Pizza sounds delicious.

217
00:11:22.279 --> 00:11:23.850
- Pizza? That's good.
- Yes! Pizza!

218
00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:28.647
- What the heck is that?
- Who puts broccoli on pizza?

219
00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:29.921
That's it. I'm done.

220
00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:32.121
Congratulations, San Francisco,

221
00:11:32.279 --> 00:11:33.379
you've ruined pizza!

222
00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:34.686
First the Hawaiians

223
00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:36.000
and now you!

224
00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:39.447
What kind of a pizza place
only serves one kind of pizza?

225
00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:41.883
Must be a
San Francisco thing, huh?

226
00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:44.220
Still, it's not as bad as that soup.

227
00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:46.288
- At that diner in Nebraska.
- Oh, yeah.

228
00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:48.740
The spoon stood up
in the soup by itself!

229
00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:50.059
That was disgusting.

230
00:11:50.159 --> 00:11:51.649
Oh, good. Family is running.

231
00:11:51.759 --> 00:11:53.080
Dad's got a steel stomach.

232
00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:54.779
The drive out was pretty fun, huh?

233
00:11:54.879 --> 00:11:56.000
What was your favorite part?

234
00:11:56.279 --> 00:11:57.644
Spitting out the car window!

235
00:11:57.759 --> 00:11:59.200
Definitely not when Dad was singing.

236
00:11:59.279 --> 00:12:00.280
Wearing a seat belt!

237
00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:02.120
Oh! What about the time
with the dinosaur?

238
00:12:02.759 --> 00:12:04.120
- Oh, that's the one.
- Definitely!

239
00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:05.640
Say cheese!

240
00:12:05.759 --> 00:12:07.220
- Dad! Dad!
- Honey!

241
00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:08.799
- Now hold still.
- The car!

242
00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:10.928
Stop! No, no, no!

243
00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:13.961
Nice one, Joy.

244
00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:15.580
I liked that time at the dinosaur.

245
00:12:15.679 --> 00:12:17.283
That was pretty funny.

246
00:12:24.559 --> 00:12:26.085
Wait. What? What happened?

247
00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:29.360
She did something to the memory.

248
00:12:30.519 --> 00:12:32.726
- What did you do?
- I just touched it.

249
00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:34.682
- That shouldn't make it change.
- Change it back, Joy!

250
00:12:34.799 --> 00:12:36.005
- I'm trying.
- You can't change it back?

251
00:12:36.159 --> 00:12:38.048
- No! I guess I can't!
- Good going, Sadness.

252
00:12:38.159 --> 00:12:39.779
Now when Riley thinks
of that moment with Dad,

253
00:12:39.879 --> 00:12:41.120
she's gonna feel sad.

254
00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:42.779
- Bravo.
- I'm sorry, Joy.

255
00:12:42.879 --> 00:12:44.120
I don't really know...

256
00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:45.684
I thought maybe if you...

257
00:12:47.519 --> 00:12:49.363
Joy, we've got a stairway coming up.

258
00:12:51.759 --> 00:12:53.019
Just don't touch any other memories

259
00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:54.559
until we figure out what's going on.

260
00:12:54.679 --> 00:12:55.726
- Okay.
- All right.

261
00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:58.048
Get ready. This is a monster railing

262
00:12:58.159 --> 00:13:00.082
and we are riding it all the way down!

263
00:13:07.519 --> 00:13:09.200
Wait, what? What happened?

264
00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:11.440
A Core Memory!

265
00:13:11.559 --> 00:13:12.561
Oh, no!

266
00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:16.840
Sadness, what are you doing?

267
00:13:16.919 --> 00:13:17.921
It looked like one was crooked

268
00:13:18.039 --> 00:13:19.928
so I opened it and then it fell out.

269
00:13:20.039 --> 00:13:21.041
I...

270
00:13:25.159 --> 00:13:26.240
Whoo-hoo!

271
00:13:26.879 --> 00:13:29.700
It's just that...
I wanted to maybe hold one.

272
00:13:29.799 --> 00:13:31.211
- Joy!
- Whoa, whoa!

273
00:13:33.399 --> 00:13:35.562
Sadness, you nearly
touched a Core Memory.

274
00:13:35.679 --> 00:13:37.980
And when you touch them,
we can't change them back.

275
00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:39.220
I know. I'm sorry.

276
00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:41.084
Something's wrong with me.

277
00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:43.088
It's like I'm having a breakdown.

278
00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:45.248
You're not having
a breakdown. It's stress.

279
00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:48.010
I keep making mistakes like that.
I'm awful.

280
00:13:48.159 --> 00:13:50.241
- No, you're not.
- And annoying.

281
00:13:50.399 --> 00:13:52.288
You know what?

282
00:13:52.399 --> 00:13:54.288
You can't focus on what's going wrong.

283
00:13:54.399 --> 00:13:56.080
There's always a way to
turn things around,

284
00:13:56.159 --> 00:13:57.605
to find the fun.

285
00:13:57.799 --> 00:13:59.484
Yeah. Find the fun.

286
00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.240
I don't know how to do that.

287
00:14:01.399 --> 00:14:02.700
Okay. Well,

288
00:14:02.799 --> 00:14:04.289
try to think of something funny.

289
00:14:04.639 --> 00:14:05.640
Um... Oh!

290
00:14:05.759 --> 00:14:08.445
Remember the funny movie
where the dog dies?

291
00:14:08.559 --> 00:14:10.482
Oh. Yeah, that's not...

292
00:14:10.679 --> 00:14:12.283
What about that time with Meg

293
00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:14.259
when Riley laughed so hard

294
00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:16.408
milk came out of her nose?

295
00:14:18.799 --> 00:14:21.259
Yeah. That hurt. It felt like fire.

296
00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:22.940
Ooh, it was awful.

297
00:14:23.039 --> 00:14:24.690
Okay, okay, don't think of that.
Let's try something else.

298
00:14:24.799 --> 00:14:26.484
Uh, what are your favorite things to do?

299
00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:27.806
My favorite?

300
00:14:27.919 --> 00:14:30.287
Um... Well, I like it
when we're outside.

301
00:14:30.399 --> 00:14:33.289
That's good. Like there's
the beach and sunshine.

302
00:14:33.399 --> 00:14:34.740
Oh! Like that time

303
00:14:34.840 --> 00:14:36.524
we buried Dad
in the sand up to his neck.

304
00:14:36.639 --> 00:14:38.846
I was thinking more like rain.

305
00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:43.460
Rain? Rain is my favorite, too!

306
00:14:43.559 --> 00:14:45.379
We can stomp around in puddles.

307
00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:48.643
You know, there's cool umbrellas,
lightning storms.

308
00:14:48.759 --> 00:14:50.759
More like when
the rain runs down our back

309
00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:52.330
and makes our shoes soggy.

310
00:14:52.879 --> 00:14:55.690
And we get all cold, shivery, and

311
00:14:55.799 --> 00:14:58.580
everything just starts
feeling droopy.

312
00:14:58.679 --> 00:15:00.807
Oh, hey, hey. Hey, easy.

313
00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:02.440
Why are you crying?

314
00:15:03.320 --> 00:15:06.004
It's just like really the opposite
of what we're going for here.

315
00:15:06.679 --> 00:15:08.648
Crying helps me slow down and obsess

316
00:15:08.799 --> 00:15:10.881
over the weight of life's problems.

317
00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:13.520
You know what? Let's, uh,

318
00:15:13.679 --> 00:15:14.940
think about something else.

319
00:15:15.039 --> 00:15:17.779
How about we read
some mind manuals, huh?

320
00:15:17.879 --> 00:15:20.042
- Sounds fun.
- I've read most of them.

321
00:15:20.159 --> 00:15:21.969
Well, have you read this one?
This seems interesting.

322
00:15:22.159 --> 00:15:25.243
"Long Term
Memory Retrieval, Volume 47"?

323
00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:27.567
- No.
- Ooh, a real page-turner!

324
00:15:27.919 --> 00:15:29.740
"Long Term Memory data selection

325
00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:31.500
"via channel subgrouping"?

326
00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:34.046
See? Fun already!
Oh, you lucky dog.

327
00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:35.519
You're reading these cool things.

328
00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:37.841
I got to go work. Life is so unfair.

329
00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:48.860
What can we do?
We've only got capital

330
00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:50.450
to last a month, maybe two.

331
00:15:51.279 --> 00:15:52.460
If we can't find investors by then,

332
00:15:52.559 --> 00:15:54.080
we're going to have to lay people off.

333
00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:56.179
Mom! Dad!

334
00:15:56.279 --> 00:15:57.644
Come kiss me good night!

335
00:15:57.759 --> 00:15:59.046
- I know. I know.
- Be right there!

336
00:15:59.159 --> 00:16:00.889
We've got to land this, okay?

337
00:16:03.559 --> 00:16:05.700
Did you hear Dad?
He sounded really upset.

338
00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:10.940
What was that?
Was it a bear? It's a bear!

339
00:16:11.039 --> 00:16:12.539
There are no bears in San Francisco.

340
00:16:12.639 --> 00:16:14.687
I saw a really hairy guy.
He looked like a bear.

341
00:16:14.799 --> 00:16:17.059
Oh, I'm so jumpy. My nerves are shot.

342
00:16:17.159 --> 00:16:18.446
Ew! I don't want to
hear about your nerves.

343
00:16:18.559 --> 00:16:21.340
I'll tell you what it is.
This move has been a bust.

344
00:16:21.440 --> 00:16:22.884
That's what I've been
telling you guys!

345
00:16:23.039 --> 00:16:25.407
There are at least 37 things for
Riley to be scared of right now.

346
00:16:25.519 --> 00:16:27.159
The smell alone is
enough to make her gag.

347
00:16:27.240 --> 00:16:29.159
I can't believe
Mom and Dad moved us here!

348
00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:31.527
Look, I get it. You guys have concerns.

349
00:16:31.679 --> 00:16:32.919
But we've been through worse!

350
00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:34.808
Tell you what,
let's make a list of all the things

351
00:16:34.919 --> 00:16:36.570
Riley should be happy about.

352
00:16:37.039 --> 00:16:39.610
Fine. Let's see, this house stinks,
our room stinks.

353
00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:41.609
- Pizza is weird here.
- Our friends are back home.

354
00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:43.403
And all of our stuff
is in the missing van!

355
00:16:43.559 --> 00:16:45.210
Oh, come on. It could be worse.

356
00:16:45.320 --> 00:16:48.210
Yeah, Joy. We could be
lying on the dirty floor. In a bag.

357
00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:50.860
Okay, I admit it, we had a rough start.

358
00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:52.450
But think of all the good things that...

359
00:16:52.559 --> 00:16:54.860
No, Joy. There's
absolutely no reason for Riley

360
00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:56.165
to be happy right now.

361
00:16:56.399 --> 00:16:57.419
Let us handle this.

362
00:16:57.519 --> 00:16:58.679
I say we skip school tomorrow

363
00:16:58.759 --> 00:16:59.899
and lock ourselves in the bedroom.

364
00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.700
We have no clean clothes.
I mean, no one should see us.

365
00:17:01.799 --> 00:17:03.440
Yeah, we could cry
until we can't breathe.

366
00:17:03.519 --> 00:17:06.220
We should lock the door
and scream that curse word we know.

367
00:17:06.319 --> 00:17:07.970
- It's a good one!
- Now hold on!

368
00:17:08.319 --> 00:17:10.099
Look, we all have our off days.

369
00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:12.259
- You know...
- Hi, honey.

370
00:17:12.359 --> 00:17:15.045
The Mom bad news train is pulling in.

371
00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:16.161
Toot-toot!

372
00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:18.163
Still no moving van.

373
00:17:18.440 --> 00:17:20.965
Now they're saying it won't be here
till Tuesday, can you believe it?

374
00:17:21.079 --> 00:17:22.126
Toot-toot-toot!

375
00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:23.969
- Where's Dad?
- On the phone.

376
00:17:24.559 --> 00:17:26.368
This new venture
is keeping him pretty busy.

377
00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:27.970
I rest my case!

378
00:17:28.079 --> 00:17:29.730
Oh, your dad's a little stressed,

379
00:17:29.839 --> 00:17:31.807
you know, about getting
his new company up and running.

380
00:17:31.920 --> 00:17:34.365
Now for a few
well-placed withering scowls.

381
00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:39.288
I guess all I really
want to say is, thank you.

382
00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:40.846
- Huh?
- You know,

383
00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:43.930
through all this confusion
you've stayed...

384
00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:46.162
Well,
you've stayed our happy girl.

385
00:17:47.519 --> 00:17:49.079
Your dad's under
a lot of pressure,

386
00:17:49.559 --> 00:17:51.900
but if you and I can keep smiling,

387
00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:53.330
it would be a big help.

388
00:17:54.039 --> 00:17:56.008
We can do that for him. Right?

389
00:17:57.279 --> 00:17:58.280
Whoa.

390
00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:00.401
Well.

391
00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:03.165
Yeah, sure.

392
00:18:03.960 --> 00:18:05.404
What did we do to deserve you?

393
00:18:09.799 --> 00:18:11.200
- Sweet dreams.
- Good night.

394
00:18:12.920 --> 00:18:14.740
Well, you can't argue
with Mom. Happy it is.

395
00:18:14.839 --> 00:18:16.171
Team Happy! Sounds great!

396
00:18:16.279 --> 00:18:17.361
Totally behind you, Joy.

397
00:18:19.039 --> 00:18:20.740
Looks like we're going into REM.

398
00:18:20.839 --> 00:18:22.259
I got Dream Duty, so I'll take care

399
00:18:22.359 --> 00:18:23.740
of sending these to Long Term.

400
00:18:23.839 --> 00:18:25.460
Great day today, guys!

401
00:18:25.559 --> 00:18:27.640
Oh, sleep well, Team Happy!

402
00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:31.367
All right, what's on tonight,
Dream Production?

403
00:18:37.319 --> 00:18:39.048
Well, this is it. The new place.

404
00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:45.007
Come live with me, Riley.

405
00:18:45.599 --> 00:18:47.409
Somebody order a broccoli pizza?

406
00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:49.005
- Eat me!
- I'm organic!

407
00:18:50.519 --> 00:18:53.842
No! Who is in charge
of programming down there?

408
00:18:54.079 --> 00:18:56.048
I know I'm not supposed
to do this, but...

409
00:19:01.359 --> 00:19:03.249
We are not going to
end the day like this.

410
00:19:47.279 --> 00:19:48.486
Don't you worry.

411
00:19:48.880 --> 00:19:52.441
I'm gonna make sure
that tomorrow is another great day.

412
00:19:53.119 --> 00:19:54.451
I promise.

413
00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:08.845
Hello! Did I wake you?

414
00:20:08.960 --> 00:20:11.166
- Do you have to play that?
- Well, I have to practice.

415
00:20:11.279 --> 00:20:13.964
And I don't think of it as playing
so much as hugging.

416
00:20:15.640 --> 00:20:16.539
Okay, first day of school!

417
00:20:16.640 --> 00:20:17.641
Very, very exciting.

418
00:20:17.759 --> 00:20:19.842
I was up late last night
figuring out a new plan.

419
00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:21.299
Here it is! Fear.

420
00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:22.845
I need a list of all the possible

421
00:20:22.960 --> 00:20:25.008
negative outcomes
on the first day at a new school.

422
00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:27.220
Way ahead of you there. Does anyone
know how to spell "meteor"?

423
00:20:27.319 --> 00:20:29.321
Disgust. Make sure
Riley stands out today.

424
00:20:29.519 --> 00:20:30.645
But also blends in.

425
00:20:30.799 --> 00:20:32.619
When I'm through,
Riley will look so good,

426
00:20:32.720 --> 00:20:34.880
the other kids will
look at their own outfits and barf.

427
00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:35.960
"Joy." "Yes, Joy?"

428
00:20:36.039 --> 00:20:37.480
"You'll be in charge of the console,

429
00:20:37.519 --> 00:20:38.900
"keeping Riley happy all day long.

430
00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:40.650
"And may I add I love
your dress? It's adorable."

431
00:20:40.759 --> 00:20:42.171
"Oh, this old thing?
Thank you so much.

432
00:20:42.279 --> 00:20:43.380
"I love the way it twirls."

433
00:20:43.480 --> 00:20:46.059
Train of Thought! Right on schedule.

434
00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:50.250
Anger. Unload the daydreams.

435
00:20:50.359 --> 00:20:52.619
I ordered extra
in case things get slow in class.

436
00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:54.688
It might come in handy.
If this new school is full of

437
00:20:54.799 --> 00:20:57.619
boring, useless classes.
Which it probably will be.

438
00:20:57.720 --> 00:21:01.361
Oh. Sadness. I have
a super important job just for you.

439
00:21:01.559 --> 00:21:03.324
- Really?
- Mmm-hmm. Follow me.

440
00:21:05.599 --> 00:21:08.125
- What are you doing?
- And there. Perfect!

441
00:21:08.319 --> 00:21:10.242
This is the circle of Sadness.

442
00:21:10.440 --> 00:21:12.140
Your job is to make sure that

443
00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:14.685
all the Sadness stays inside of it.

444
00:21:15.079 --> 00:21:17.619
So you want me to just stand here?

445
00:21:17.720 --> 00:21:20.529
Hey, it's not my place to
tell you how to do your job.

446
00:21:20.680 --> 00:21:24.048
Just make sure that all the Sadness

447
00:21:24.160 --> 00:21:25.365
stays in the circle!

448
00:21:25.519 --> 00:21:28.619
See? You're a pro at this!
Isn't this fun?

449
00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:29.779
- No.
- Atta girl.

450
00:21:29.880 --> 00:21:31.099
All right, everyone, fresh start.

451
00:21:31.200 --> 00:21:33.339
We are gonna have a good day,
which will turn into a good week,

452
00:21:33.440 --> 00:21:34.539
which will turn into a good year,

453
00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:35.799
which turns into a good life!

454
00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:39.083
So, the big day!
New school, new friends, huh?

455
00:21:39.200 --> 00:21:41.406
I know! I'm kind of nervous,
but I'm mostly excited.

456
00:21:41.519 --> 00:21:43.089
How do I look? Do you like my shirt?

457
00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:44.530
Very cute!

458
00:21:44.880 --> 00:21:46.460
Are you gonna be okay?
You want us to walk with you?

459
00:21:46.559 --> 00:21:49.006
Mom and Dad? With us in public?
No thank you.

460
00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:50.200
Uh... I'm on it!

461
00:21:50.279 --> 00:21:52.442
Nope! I'm fine. Bye, Mom. Bye, Dad.

462
00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:54.000
Have a good day at school, monkey.

463
00:21:59.440 --> 00:22:00.930
Have a great day, sweetheart!

464
00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:03.160
That's crazy. It really is.

465
00:22:03.200 --> 00:22:04.279
That was so funny.

466
00:22:05.240 --> 00:22:07.240
Do you know
what basketball game is coming up?

467
00:22:08.079 --> 00:22:09.080
Are you sure we want to do this?

468
00:22:09.200 --> 00:22:12.170
- In we go!
- Okay! Going in! Yes!

469
00:22:16.720 --> 00:22:17.740
Did you see her? Hello!

470
00:22:17.839 --> 00:22:19.700
Okay, we've got
a group of cool girls at two o'clock.

471
00:22:19.799 --> 00:22:21.131
- How do you know?
- Double ears pierced,

472
00:22:21.240 --> 00:22:22.287
infinity scarf.

473
00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:23.660
Whoa. Is she wearing eye shadow?

474
00:22:23.759 --> 00:22:25.740
- Yeah, we want to be friends with them.
- Let's go talk to them!

475
00:22:25.839 --> 00:22:27.579
Are you kidding?
We're not talking to them.

476
00:22:27.680 --> 00:22:28.920
We want them to like us.

477
00:22:29.039 --> 00:22:30.371
Oh. Yeah. Wait, what?

478
00:22:30.480 --> 00:22:32.288
Almost finished
with the potential disasters.

479
00:22:32.400 --> 00:22:34.579
Worst scenario is either quicksand,

480
00:22:34.680 --> 00:22:36.090
spontaneous combustion,

481
00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:37.849
or getting called on by the teacher.

482
00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:39.220
So as long as none of those happen...

483
00:22:39.319 --> 00:22:41.891
Okay, everybody.
We have a new student in class today.

484
00:22:42.039 --> 00:22:44.019
Are you kidding me? Out of the gate?

485
00:22:44.119 --> 00:22:45.166
This is not happening!

486
00:22:45.440 --> 00:22:48.099
Riley, would you like
to tell us something about yourself?

487
00:22:48.200 --> 00:22:50.327
No! Pretend we can't speak English.

488
00:22:50.440 --> 00:22:51.645
Don't worry. I got this.

489
00:22:52.759 --> 00:22:54.250
Uh... Okay.

490
00:22:54.759 --> 00:22:56.339
My name is Riley Andersen.

491
00:22:56.440 --> 00:22:59.648
I'm from Minnesota and now I live here.

492
00:23:01.960 --> 00:23:04.201
And how about Minnesota?

493
00:23:04.319 --> 00:23:05.579
Can you tell us something about it?

494
00:23:05.680 --> 00:23:07.921
Well, you certainly
get a lot more snow than we do.

495
00:23:10.240 --> 00:23:11.890
She's hilarious!

496
00:23:13.559 --> 00:23:15.059
Yeah, it gets pretty cold.

497
00:23:15.160 --> 00:23:16.161
The lake freezes over,

498
00:23:16.279 --> 00:23:17.619
and that's when we play hockey.

499
00:23:17.720 --> 00:23:19.847
I'm on a great team.
We're called the Prairie Dogs.

500
00:23:20.119 --> 00:23:22.726
My friend Meg plays forward.
And my dad's the coach.

501
00:23:23.480 --> 00:23:25.642
Pretty much everyone
in my family skates.

502
00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:27.330
It's kind of a family tradition.

503
00:23:27.440 --> 00:23:29.203
We go out on the lake
almost every weekend.

504
00:23:32.200 --> 00:23:34.964
Or we did, till I moved away.

505
00:23:35.079 --> 00:23:36.319
- Hey, what gives?
- Wait, what?

506
00:23:36.559 --> 00:23:40.041
Hey, Sadness! You touched
a memory? We talked about this.

507
00:23:40.160 --> 00:23:41.888
Oh, yeah, I know. I'm sorry.

508
00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:45.048
Get back in your circle.
What's going on?

509
00:23:45.160 --> 00:23:47.079
- Why won't it eject?
- Get it out of there, Joy.

510
00:23:47.200 --> 00:23:49.567
We used
to play tag and stuff.

511
00:23:49.680 --> 00:23:51.200
Cool kids whispering at three o'clock!

512
00:23:51.480 --> 00:23:52.460
- Did you see that look?
- Oh, no.

513
00:23:52.559 --> 00:23:53.560
They're judging us!

514
00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:57.366
Somebody help me!
Grab that... Everybody put...

515
00:23:57.799 --> 00:23:59.847
But everything's different now.

516
00:24:00.680 --> 00:24:01.727
Since we moved.

517
00:24:04.400 --> 00:24:07.688
Oh, no! We're crying! At school!

518
00:24:07.839 --> 00:24:10.126
What? Sadness! What are you doing?

519
00:24:11.160 --> 00:24:13.401
Oh, no! Oh, I'm sorry!

520
00:24:13.759 --> 00:24:14.807
Huh?

521
00:24:14.960 --> 00:24:16.689
It's a Core Memory!

522
00:24:16.880 --> 00:24:18.290
But it's blue.

523
00:24:20.039 --> 00:24:23.521
No! Wait! Stop it! No! Ah! No!

524
00:24:30.680 --> 00:24:31.806
Joy, no.

525
00:24:32.000 --> 00:24:33.411
- That's a Core Memory!
- Hey!

526
00:24:33.519 --> 00:24:34.726
- Joy, wait!
- Stop it! Let go!

527
00:24:35.480 --> 00:24:37.049
Ah! The Core Memories!

528
00:24:51.960 --> 00:24:53.121
No, no, no, no!

529
00:24:56.559 --> 00:24:58.642
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

530
00:25:06.440 --> 00:25:07.770
Thank you, Riley.

531
00:25:07.920 --> 00:25:10.320
I know it can be tough
moving to a new place,

532
00:25:10.440 --> 00:25:12.203
but we're happy to have you here.

533
00:25:12.920 --> 00:25:14.980
All right, everyone,
get out your history books

534
00:25:15.079 --> 00:25:16.650
and turn to chapter seven.

535
00:25:19.359 --> 00:25:20.963
Can I say that curse word now?

536
00:25:38.720 --> 00:25:40.801
Ah!

537
00:25:42.160 --> 00:25:45.323
Oh, no! One, two, three. Okay.

538
00:25:46.640 --> 00:25:49.802
I got them. Where are we?

539
00:25:50.960 --> 00:25:53.201
Long Term Memory? Wait...

540
00:25:59.799 --> 00:26:01.325
Goofball Island?

541
00:26:02.599 --> 00:26:04.539
Riley's Islands of Personality.

542
00:26:04.640 --> 00:26:06.164
They're all down!

543
00:26:07.000 --> 00:26:08.843
Oh! This is bad.

544
00:26:09.000 --> 00:26:11.001
We... We can fix this!

545
00:26:11.640 --> 00:26:13.403
We just have to
get back to Headquarters,

546
00:26:13.559 --> 00:26:14.980
plug the Core Memories in,

547
00:26:15.079 --> 00:26:16.763
and Riley will be back to normal.

548
00:26:17.920 --> 00:26:20.140
Riley has no Core Memories.

549
00:26:20.240 --> 00:26:22.321
No Personality Islands and no...

550
00:26:23.559 --> 00:26:24.641
What? What is it?

551
00:26:24.839 --> 00:26:25.840
You.

552
00:26:26.000 --> 00:26:27.763
You're not in Headquarters.

553
00:26:27.880 --> 00:26:30.530
Without you, Riley can't be happy.

554
00:26:31.200 --> 00:26:32.804
We got to get you back up there.

555
00:26:33.519 --> 00:26:34.806
I'm coming, Riley.

556
00:26:49.039 --> 00:26:51.180
So, as it turns out, the green trash can

557
00:26:51.279 --> 00:26:53.259
is not recycling, it's for greens.

558
00:26:53.359 --> 00:26:54.963
- Like compost. And eggshells.
- Mmm.

559
00:26:55.079 --> 00:26:56.683
And the blue one is recycling.

560
00:26:56.839 --> 00:26:58.700
- And the black one is trash.
- Riley is acting so weird.

561
00:26:58.799 --> 00:26:59.880
Why is she acting so weird?

562
00:26:59.920 --> 00:27:02.207
What do you expect?
All the Islands are down.

563
00:27:02.319 --> 00:27:03.366
Joy would know what to do.

564
00:27:03.480 --> 00:27:04.641
That's it.

565
00:27:04.759 --> 00:27:07.444
Until she gets back,
we just do what Joy would do!

566
00:27:07.599 --> 00:27:10.285
Great idea. Anger, Fear, Disgust,

567
00:27:10.559 --> 00:27:11.891
how are we supposed to be happy?

568
00:27:12.400 --> 00:27:14.402
Hey, Riley. I've got good news!

569
00:27:14.559 --> 00:27:17.380
I found a junior hockey league
right here in San Francisco.

570
00:27:17.480 --> 00:27:19.448
And get this: Try-outs are tomorrow

571
00:27:19.559 --> 00:27:21.449
after school. What luck, right?

572
00:27:21.559 --> 00:27:22.859
- Hockey?
- Uh-oh. What do we do?

573
00:27:22.960 --> 00:27:24.484
Guys, this is...

574
00:27:24.599 --> 00:27:25.726
You pretend to be Joy.

575
00:27:25.839 --> 00:27:27.729
Won't it be great to be
back out on the ice?

576
00:27:29.720 --> 00:27:31.961
Oh, yeah, that sounds fantastic.

577
00:27:32.920 --> 00:27:34.729
What was that?
That wasn't anything like Joy!

578
00:27:34.920 --> 00:27:37.082
- Uh, because I'm not Joy.
- Yeah, no kidding.

579
00:27:39.400 --> 00:27:40.640
Did you guys pick up on that?

580
00:27:40.759 --> 00:27:42.460
- Mmm-hmm. Something's wrong.
- Totally.

581
00:27:42.559 --> 00:27:43.799
Should we ask her?

582
00:27:43.920 --> 00:27:45.604
Let's probe. But keep it subtle,

583
00:27:45.720 --> 00:27:46.767
so she doesn't notice.

584
00:27:47.079 --> 00:27:49.048
So, how was the first day of school?

585
00:27:49.279 --> 00:27:50.299
She's probing us.

586
00:27:50.400 --> 00:27:51.700
I'm done. You pretend to be Joy.

587
00:27:51.799 --> 00:27:54.166
What? Okay. Um, hmm.

588
00:27:54.599 --> 00:27:57.604
It was fine, I guess. I don't know.

589
00:27:57.720 --> 00:28:00.404
Oh. Very smooth.
That was just like Joy.

590
00:28:00.720 --> 00:28:02.539
Something is definitely going on.

591
00:28:02.640 --> 00:28:05.040
She's never acted like this before.
What should we do?

592
00:28:05.440 --> 00:28:06.660
We're going to
find out what's happening.

593
00:28:06.759 --> 00:28:08.019
But we'll need support.

594
00:28:08.119 --> 00:28:09.121
Signal the husband.

595
00:28:10.119 --> 00:28:11.166
Ahem!

596
00:28:12.799 --> 00:28:14.882
With a nice
pass over to Reeves,

597
00:28:15.119 --> 00:28:16.280
comes across ...and nice!

598
00:28:19.920 --> 00:28:23.380
Uh-oh. She's looking at us.
Uh, what did she say?

599
00:28:23.480 --> 00:28:25.800
What? Oh! Sorry, sir.
No one was listening.

600
00:28:26.119 --> 00:28:28.180
Is it garbage night?
We left the toilet seat up?

601
00:28:28.279 --> 00:28:30.088
What? What is it, woman? What?

602
00:28:30.319 --> 00:28:32.322
Ugh, he's making
that stupid face again.

603
00:28:32.480 --> 00:28:34.243
I could strangle
him right now.

604
00:28:34.480 --> 00:28:35.527
Signal him again.

605
00:28:38.200 --> 00:28:40.931
Ah! So, Riley, how was school?

606
00:28:41.079 --> 00:28:42.923
- You got to be kidding me!
- Seriously?

607
00:28:43.039 --> 00:28:45.884
For this we gave up
that Brazilian helicopter pilot?

608
00:28:46.400 --> 00:28:47.845
Move! I'll be Joy.

609
00:28:48.359 --> 00:28:50.044
School was great, all right?

610
00:28:50.359 --> 00:28:52.202
Riley. Is everything okay?

611
00:28:52.480 --> 00:28:53.480
Ugh!

612
00:28:53.759 --> 00:28:55.329
Sir, she just rolled her eyes at us.

613
00:28:55.599 --> 00:28:56.885
What is her deal?

614
00:28:57.079 --> 00:28:58.683
All right, make a show of force.

615
00:28:58.839 --> 00:29:00.285
I don't want to have to
put "the foot" down.

616
00:29:00.400 --> 00:29:02.323
No, not the foot!

617
00:29:02.519 --> 00:29:04.567
Riley, I do not like this new attitude.

618
00:29:04.799 --> 00:29:06.380
Oh, I'll show you attitude, old man.

619
00:29:06.480 --> 00:29:07.845
No. No, no, no! Stay happy!

620
00:29:08.599 --> 00:29:10.728
What is your problem?
Just leave me alone!

621
00:29:10.839 --> 00:29:12.568
Sir, reporting high levels of sass!

622
00:29:13.039 --> 00:29:14.529
Take it to DEFCON Two.

623
00:29:14.640 --> 00:29:16.660
You heard that, gentlemen. DEFCON Two.

624
00:29:17.960 --> 00:29:19.420
Listen, young lady,
I don't know where...

625
00:29:19.519 --> 00:29:21.521
...this disrespectful
attitude came from...

626
00:29:21.640 --> 00:29:23.085
You want a piece of this, pops?

627
00:29:23.240 --> 00:29:24.365
Come and get it!

628
00:29:24.559 --> 00:29:26.005
Yeah, well... Well...

629
00:29:26.240 --> 00:29:28.367
Here it comes. Prepare the foot!

630
00:29:29.960 --> 00:29:31.371
Keys to safety position.

631
00:29:33.319 --> 00:29:34.759
Ready to launch
on your command, sir!

632
00:29:37.559 --> 00:29:39.085
Just shut up!

633
00:29:40.240 --> 00:29:41.365
Fire!

634
00:29:41.880 --> 00:29:45.406
That's it! Go to your room! Now!

635
00:29:45.519 --> 00:29:46.520
Uh!

636
00:29:48.960 --> 00:29:51.566
The foot is down!
The foot is down!

637
00:29:53.079 --> 00:29:54.660
Good job, gentlemen.

638
00:29:54.759 --> 00:29:56.285
That could have been a disaster.

639
00:29:57.119 --> 00:29:58.565
Well, that was a disaster.

640
00:30:02.039 --> 00:30:04.849
Come fly with me, gatinha.

641
00:30:17.240 --> 00:30:19.685
We're going to walk out there? On that?

642
00:30:20.079 --> 00:30:21.730
It's the quickest way back.

643
00:30:21.839 --> 00:30:23.729
But it's right over the Memory Dump.

644
00:30:23.920 --> 00:30:26.082
If we fall, we'll be forgotten forever.

645
00:30:26.400 --> 00:30:30.121
We have to do this for Riley.
Just follow my footsteps.

646
00:30:30.240 --> 00:30:31.651
- Oh, okay.
- It's not that high.

647
00:30:31.759 --> 00:30:33.682
It's totally fine...

648
00:30:42.119 --> 00:30:43.201
No!

649
00:30:49.920 --> 00:30:51.000
Hey.

650
00:30:51.920 --> 00:30:54.923
So, uh, things got a little
out of hand downstairs.

651
00:30:55.960 --> 00:30:57.290
Do you want to talk about it?

652
00:30:58.839 --> 00:31:01.047
Come on, where's my happy girl?

653
00:31:02.799 --> 00:31:04.608
Monkey.

654
00:31:04.960 --> 00:31:06.883
Oh, he's trying to start up Goofball.

655
00:31:07.960 --> 00:31:08.961
Come on!

656
00:31:19.640 --> 00:31:20.641
Ah!

657
00:31:21.680 --> 00:31:23.125
Go back! Run, run, run!

658
00:31:51.319 --> 00:31:52.401
What...

659
00:32:08.039 --> 00:32:10.691
I get it. You need some alone time.

660
00:32:13.640 --> 00:32:14.846
We'll talk later.

661
00:32:18.680 --> 00:32:20.099
We have a major problem.

662
00:32:20.200 --> 00:32:22.123
Oh, Joy, where are you?

663
00:32:23.519 --> 00:32:25.567
We lost Goofball Island.

664
00:32:26.279 --> 00:32:27.724
That means she can lose Friendship

665
00:32:27.880 --> 00:32:30.041
and Hockey and Honesty and Family.

666
00:32:31.160 --> 00:32:32.923
You can fix this, right, Joy?

667
00:32:33.680 --> 00:32:36.365
I, uh... I don't know.

668
00:32:36.480 --> 00:32:38.163
- Oh...
- But we have to try.

669
00:32:38.359 --> 00:32:39.441
Okay, come on.

670
00:32:40.839 --> 00:32:42.729
- Riley's gone to sleep.
- Oh...

671
00:32:42.839 --> 00:32:45.319
Which is a good thing.

672
00:32:45.480 --> 00:32:46.720
When you think about it because

673
00:32:46.799 --> 00:32:48.847
nothing else bad
can happen while she's asleep.

674
00:32:48.960 --> 00:32:51.008
We'll be back to Headquarters
before she wakes up.

675
00:32:51.200 --> 00:32:53.567
We'll just go across Friendship Island.

676
00:32:56.039 --> 00:32:57.339
Oh, we'll never make it.

677
00:32:57.440 --> 00:32:58.520
- Oh, no!
- No, no, no!

678
00:32:58.720 --> 00:33:00.220
Don't obsess over
the weight of life's problems.

679
00:33:00.319 --> 00:33:02.209
Remember the funny movie
where the dog dies?

680
00:33:02.359 --> 00:33:04.839
Oh, Sadness,
we don't have time for this.

681
00:33:04.960 --> 00:33:08.123
We'll just have to go around.
Take the scenic route.

682
00:33:08.559 --> 00:33:10.926
Wait, Joy,
you could get lost in there!

683
00:33:11.240 --> 00:33:12.570
Think positive!

684
00:33:12.799 --> 00:33:16.122
Okay. I'm positive
you will get lost in there.

685
00:33:16.759 --> 00:33:18.443
That's Long Term Memory.

686
00:33:18.960 --> 00:33:21.122
An endless warren
of corridors and shelves.

687
00:33:21.240 --> 00:33:22.809
I read about it in the manuals.

688
00:33:23.799 --> 00:33:25.369
The manuals?

689
00:33:25.559 --> 00:33:26.606
The manuals!

690
00:33:26.720 --> 00:33:28.500
- You read the manuals!
- Yeah.

691
00:33:28.599 --> 00:33:30.567
So you know the way
back to Headquarters!

692
00:33:31.000 --> 00:33:32.080
I guess.

693
00:33:32.200 --> 00:33:34.009
Ooh!

694
00:33:35.000 --> 00:33:36.080
You are my map!

695
00:33:36.359 --> 00:33:38.579
Let's go! Lead on, my map!

696
00:33:38.680 --> 00:33:39.740
Show me where we're going!

697
00:33:39.839 --> 00:33:43.579
Okay. Only I'm too sad to walk.

698
00:33:43.680 --> 00:33:46.411
Just give me a few... hours.

699
00:33:46.640 --> 00:33:47.686
Ooh!

700
00:33:48.440 --> 00:33:49.487
Which way? Left?

701
00:33:49.640 --> 00:33:50.721
Right.

702
00:33:51.119 --> 00:33:52.380
No. I mean, go left.

703
00:33:52.480 --> 00:33:54.323
I said left was right. Like "correct."

704
00:33:54.440 --> 00:33:55.566
Okay.

705
00:33:55.799 --> 00:33:57.689
This actually
feels kind of nice.

706
00:33:58.039 --> 00:33:59.619
Okay, here we go!

707
00:33:59.720 --> 00:34:01.801
We'll be back to Headquarters
before morning.

708
00:34:01.920 --> 00:34:05.366
We can do it! This will be easy!
This is working!

709
00:34:08.719 --> 00:34:11.291
This is not working.
Are we getting close?

710
00:34:11.480 --> 00:34:12.969
Yeah, just another right.

711
00:34:13.760 --> 00:34:18.208
And... a left and then
another... left and...

712
00:34:18.320 --> 00:34:20.900
Uh, are you sure
you know where we're going?

713
00:34:21.000 --> 00:34:23.731
Because we seem to be
walking away from Headquarters.

714
00:34:24.840 --> 00:34:26.648
Riley's awake.

715
00:34:26.960 --> 00:34:28.121
Ooh! Oh!

716
00:34:30.599 --> 00:34:32.045
Don't touch. Remember?

717
00:34:32.159 --> 00:34:34.639
If you touch them, they stay sad.

718
00:34:34.800 --> 00:34:38.121
Oh, sorry, I won't. Starting now.

719
00:34:38.239 --> 00:34:40.447
Oh, I can't take much more of this.

720
00:34:40.679 --> 00:34:41.885
Forget them!

721
00:34:42.159 --> 00:34:43.161
Mind workers!

722
00:34:43.280 --> 00:34:44.405
But, Joy, we're almost...

723
00:34:46.000 --> 00:34:47.001
Phone numbers.

724
00:34:47.159 --> 00:34:48.684
We don't need all these.
They're in her phone.

725
00:34:48.800 --> 00:34:51.239
- Excuse me, hi.
- Just forget all of that. Please. Forget it!

726
00:34:52.440 --> 00:34:53.940
- I need to find Friendship Island.
- Look at this.

727
00:34:54.039 --> 00:34:55.690
Four years of piano lessons.

728
00:34:55.840 --> 00:34:56.840
Yeah,
it looks pretty faded.

729
00:34:56.960 --> 00:34:58.371
You know what? Save Chopsticks

730
00:34:58.480 --> 00:35:00.079
and Heart and Soul, get rid of the rest.

731
00:35:00.519 --> 00:35:01.940
- Are you...
- US Presidents. What do you think?

732
00:35:02.039 --> 00:35:04.079
Yeah, just keep
Washington, Lincoln and the fat one.

733
00:35:04.199 --> 00:35:05.360
- Forget 'em!
- Hey!

734
00:35:05.480 --> 00:35:06.579
You can't throw those away!

735
00:35:06.679 --> 00:35:07.760
Those are perfectly good memories.

736
00:35:08.000 --> 00:35:10.260
The names of
every "Cutie Pie Princess" doll?

737
00:35:10.360 --> 00:35:12.099
Yes! That is critical information!

738
00:35:12.199 --> 00:35:13.480
Glitterstorm, Honeypants...

739
00:35:13.559 --> 00:35:14.606
Forget 'em!

740
00:35:19.800 --> 00:35:20.860
Hey! Bring those back!

741
00:35:20.960 --> 00:35:23.079
They're in the dump. Nothing
comes back from the dump.

742
00:35:23.199 --> 00:35:24.659
Yeah. Look, lady, this is our job, okay?

743
00:35:24.760 --> 00:35:26.887
When Riley doesn't care
about a memory, it fades.

744
00:35:27.079 --> 00:35:28.605
- Fades?
- Happens to the best of them.

745
00:35:28.760 --> 00:35:32.242
Yeah, except for this bad boy.
This one will never fade.

746
00:35:32.719 --> 00:35:34.688
<i>- ? TripleDent gum</i>
<i>- ? Will make you smile ?</i>

747
00:35:34.840 --> 00:35:36.204
The song
from the gum commercial?

748
00:35:36.320 --> 00:35:37.320
You know, sometimes we send that one

749
00:35:37.440 --> 00:35:38.440
up to Headquarters for no reason.

750
00:35:38.559 --> 00:35:41.019
It just plays in Riley's head
over and over again.

751
00:35:41.119 --> 00:35:42.610
Like a million times!

752
00:35:42.800 --> 00:35:44.005
Let's watch it again!

753
00:35:44.199 --> 00:35:45.260
<i>? TripleDent gum ?</i>

754
00:35:45.360 --> 00:35:47.248
Yeah, I know. We all know the song.

755
00:35:47.360 --> 00:35:48.699
Okay. Yeah, real catchy. Okay.

756
00:35:48.800 --> 00:35:49.780
Hey, what do you think? Should we do it?

757
00:35:49.880 --> 00:35:50.880
Yeah!

758
00:35:51.079 --> 00:35:52.570
Okay, here we go!

759
00:35:55.920 --> 00:35:56.920
<i>? TripleDent gum ?</i>

760
00:35:57.000 --> 00:35:58.364
What the... This again?

761
00:35:59.880 --> 00:36:02.086
Wait! Do you know how to
get to Friendship Island?

762
00:36:02.519 --> 00:36:03.567
<i>? TripleDent gum ?</i>

763
00:36:03.719 --> 00:36:05.719
Do you like it there?
Did you feel any earthquakes?

764
00:36:05.760 --> 00:36:06.760
Is the bridge cool?

765
00:36:07.000 --> 00:36:08.239
Yeah, it's good.

766
00:36:08.440 --> 00:36:09.521
What happened with the playoffs?

767
00:36:09.639 --> 00:36:10.659
We won the first game.

768
00:36:10.760 --> 00:36:12.960
Coach says we might actually
go to the finals this year.

769
00:36:13.039 --> 00:36:14.659
Oh, and we've got
this new girl on the team.

770
00:36:14.760 --> 00:36:15.885
She's so cool.

771
00:36:16.000 --> 00:36:17.579
Uh, she did not just say that.

772
00:36:17.679 --> 00:36:19.920
A new girl? Meg has
a new friend already?

773
00:36:20.039 --> 00:36:22.088
Hey, hey! Stay happy!

774
00:36:22.280 --> 00:36:24.280
We do not want to lose
any more islands here, guys!

775
00:36:24.480 --> 00:36:25.481
We can pass the puck to each other

776
00:36:25.599 --> 00:36:27.967
without even looking.
It's like mind reading!

777
00:36:28.280 --> 00:36:29.485
You like to read minds, Meg?

778
00:36:29.599 --> 00:36:31.320
I got something
for you to read, right here!

779
00:36:31.400 --> 00:36:32.420
Let's just be calm for one second! Ahhh!

780
00:36:33.760 --> 00:36:35.204
- I heard they have parrots...
- I've got to go.

781
00:36:35.400 --> 00:36:36.731
- What?
- I got to go!

782
00:36:38.000 --> 00:36:39.445
Okay, could you just please
tell me which way is...

783
00:36:41.239 --> 00:36:42.320
Oh, no!

784
00:36:45.639 --> 00:36:47.324
Friendship Island! What?

785
00:36:58.639 --> 00:37:00.324
Oh, not Friendship.

786
00:37:06.400 --> 00:37:10.724
Oh, Riley loved that one.
And now it's gone.

787
00:37:11.280 --> 00:37:12.539
Goodbye, friendship.

788
00:37:12.639 --> 00:37:14.164
Hello, loneliness.

789
00:37:18.719 --> 00:37:20.960
We'll just have to go the long way.

790
00:37:21.480 --> 00:37:26.007
Yeah. The long, long, long, long way.

791
00:37:27.159 --> 00:37:28.320
I'm ready.

792
00:37:28.719 --> 00:37:31.690
There's got to be a better way.

793
00:37:34.039 --> 00:37:35.659
Ooh! Look at you!

794
00:37:35.760 --> 00:37:36.760
Huh?

795
00:37:37.000 --> 00:37:39.400
I will take you, but not you.

796
00:37:39.679 --> 00:37:41.681
Oh, who am I kidding? I can't leave you.

797
00:37:42.280 --> 00:37:43.769
Hello!

798
00:37:43.960 --> 00:37:45.121
Wait! Hey! Wait!

799
00:37:47.519 --> 00:37:48.681
Oh, wait! Stop!

800
00:37:57.639 --> 00:37:58.766
- Excuse me.
- Ah!

801
00:37:59.599 --> 00:38:02.409
Uh, I was looking for, um... Diversion!

802
00:38:02.519 --> 00:38:04.340
- What?
- Ha-ha! So long, sucker!

803
00:38:05.880 --> 00:38:07.119
Ow, I hurt all over.

804
00:38:07.159 --> 00:38:08.730
Wait. I know you.

805
00:38:08.880 --> 00:38:10.688
No, you don't. I get that a lot.

806
00:38:11.320 --> 00:38:12.340
I look like a lot of people.

807
00:38:12.440 --> 00:38:14.090
No, no, no. I do.

808
00:38:14.199 --> 00:38:16.771
Bing Bong! Riley's imaginary friend!

809
00:38:16.880 --> 00:38:19.326
- You really do know me?
- Well, of course!

810
00:38:19.480 --> 00:38:21.880
Riley loved playing with you!
You two are best friends!

811
00:38:22.039 --> 00:38:23.460
Oh! Oh, you would know.

812
00:38:23.559 --> 00:38:24.780
We're trying to get
back to Headquarters.

813
00:38:24.880 --> 00:38:26.882
Headquarters? You guys
are from Headquarters?

814
00:38:27.039 --> 00:38:29.610
Well, yeah. I'm Joy. This is Sadness.

815
00:38:29.880 --> 00:38:31.768
- You're Joy? The Joy?
Mmm-hmm.

816
00:38:31.880 --> 00:38:33.405
What the heck are you doing out here?

817
00:38:33.519 --> 00:38:35.619
That's a good question.
You want to answer that, Sadness?

818
00:38:35.719 --> 00:38:38.724
Wow. Without you,
Riley won't ever be happy.

819
00:38:38.840 --> 00:38:41.126
We can't have that.
We got to get you back.

820
00:38:41.239 --> 00:38:42.539
I'll tell you what. Follow me!

821
00:38:42.639 --> 00:38:44.085
Oh, thank you!

822
00:38:44.320 --> 00:38:45.969
It is so great to see you again.

823
00:38:46.079 --> 00:38:48.242
I gotta tell you, I am such
a huge fan of your work.

824
00:38:48.400 --> 00:38:50.739
Do you remember when you
and Riley were in a band?

825
00:38:50.840 --> 00:38:53.380
I went to all of your concerts.

826
00:38:53.480 --> 00:38:54.739
Yeah, I blow a mean nose.

827
00:38:54.840 --> 00:38:56.409
Watching you play tag
was such a treat.

828
00:38:56.559 --> 00:38:57.925
Two-time world champ.

829
00:38:58.039 --> 00:38:59.530
Oh! And remember your rockets?

830
00:38:59.639 --> 00:39:01.688
Of course!
It runs on song power!

831
00:39:02.000 --> 00:39:03.445
That's right! Your theme song!

832
00:39:03.559 --> 00:39:04.800
<i>? Who's your friend who likes to play?</i>

833
00:39:04.920 --> 00:39:06.126
<i>? Bing Bong
Bing Bong</i>

834
00:39:06.280 --> 00:39:07.610
<i>? His rocket makes you yell "Hooray!"</i>

835
00:39:07.760 --> 00:39:09.045
<i>? Bing Bong, Bing Bong ?</i>

836
00:39:09.639 --> 00:39:11.860
What exactly are you supposed to be?

837
00:39:11.960 --> 00:39:14.500
You know, it's unclear.
I'm mostly cotton candy.

838
00:39:14.599 --> 00:39:19.288
But shape-wise I'm part cat,
part elephant, part dolphin.

839
00:39:19.559 --> 00:39:20.686
Dolphin?

840
00:39:23.559 --> 00:39:25.019
You got to remember,
when Riley was three,

841
00:39:25.119 --> 00:39:26.485
animals were all the rage.

842
00:39:26.599 --> 00:39:28.284
The cow goes moo.
The horse goes neigh.

843
00:39:28.559 --> 00:39:29.940
That's all people talked
about back then.

844
00:39:30.039 --> 00:39:31.451
Yeah. Yeah. I guess that's true.

845
00:39:31.599 --> 00:39:32.619
What are you doing out here?

846
00:39:32.719 --> 00:39:36.121
Well, there's not much call
for imaginary friends lately.

847
00:39:36.239 --> 00:39:38.606
So, uh, I, you know, um...

848
00:39:40.480 --> 00:39:42.608
Hey, hey. Don't be sad.

849
00:39:42.920 --> 00:39:44.967
Tell you what. When I get
back up to Headquarters,

850
00:39:45.079 --> 00:39:46.809
I'll make sure Riley remembers you.

851
00:39:47.119 --> 00:39:48.420
- You will?
- Of course!

852
00:39:48.519 --> 00:39:50.579
She'd love that.

853
00:39:50.679 --> 00:39:52.860
This is the greatest day of my life!

854
00:39:52.960 --> 00:39:54.688
Ha, cha, cha, cha, cha. Ow!

855
00:39:54.800 --> 00:39:56.860
Ow, ow, ow, ow!

856
00:39:56.960 --> 00:39:58.166
Oh, are you okay?

857
00:39:58.599 --> 00:39:59.726
Hey, what's going on?

858
00:39:59.920 --> 00:40:01.460
I cry candy.

859
00:40:01.559 --> 00:40:03.059
Try the caramel. It's delicious.

860
00:40:03.159 --> 00:40:04.490
Ooh. Whoa!

861
00:40:05.039 --> 00:40:06.619
Ooh, here, use this.

862
00:40:06.719 --> 00:40:08.320
- Thanks!
- Whoa, hold on, wait a second.

863
00:40:12.039 --> 00:40:13.804
It always gets stuck at the bottom.

864
00:40:16.480 --> 00:40:19.324
Here. What? It's imaginary.

865
00:40:19.719 --> 00:40:21.528
Thanks. This will make it a lot easier

866
00:40:21.639 --> 00:40:22.686
to walk back to Headquarters.

867
00:40:22.800 --> 00:40:24.324
Walk? We're not walking.

868
00:40:24.599 --> 00:40:26.648
We're taking the Train of Thought!

869
00:40:28.360 --> 00:40:30.099
The train, of course!

870
00:40:30.199 --> 00:40:32.780
That is so much faster!
But how do we catch it?

871
00:40:32.880 --> 00:40:34.563
Well, it kind of goes
all over the place,

872
00:40:34.679 --> 00:40:36.360
but there is a station
in Imagination Land.

873
00:40:37.280 --> 00:40:39.601
I know a shortcut.
Come on, this way!

874
00:40:39.960 --> 00:40:42.121
Oh, I am so glad we ran into you!

875
00:40:42.679 --> 00:40:45.251
The station is right
through here. After you.

876
00:40:45.480 --> 00:40:46.606
- Joy.
- What?

877
00:40:46.800 --> 00:40:48.403
I read about this place

878
00:40:48.519 --> 00:40:50.123
in the manual. We shouldn't go in there.

879
00:40:50.280 --> 00:40:52.202
Bing Bong says
it's the quickest way to Headquarters.

880
00:40:52.320 --> 00:40:54.367
No, but, Joy, this is abstract thought.

881
00:40:54.480 --> 00:40:55.559
What are you talking about?

882
00:40:55.679 --> 00:40:58.411
I go in here all the time.
It's a shortcut, you see?

883
00:40:58.599 --> 00:41:02.206
D-A-N-G-E-R. Shortcut.
I'll prove it to you.

884
00:41:03.360 --> 00:41:06.204
Look at me. I'm closer to the station

885
00:41:06.440 --> 00:41:08.204
because I'm taking the shortcut.

886
00:41:08.679 --> 00:41:10.568
Let's go around. This way.

887
00:41:10.679 --> 00:41:12.250
Almost there!

888
00:41:13.320 --> 00:41:15.659
If you want to walk
the long way, go for it.

889
00:41:15.760 --> 00:41:17.728
But Riley needs to be happy.

890
00:41:17.880 --> 00:41:19.291
I'm not missing that train.

891
00:41:19.480 --> 00:41:20.760
Bing Bong knows what he's doing.

892
00:41:20.880 --> 00:41:22.768
He's part dolphin.
They're very smart.

893
00:41:22.920 --> 00:41:24.570
Well, I guess.

894
00:41:27.519 --> 00:41:29.362
- What did you get?
- I don't know.

895
00:41:43.400 --> 00:41:45.083
Okay, what abstract concept

896
00:41:45.199 --> 00:41:46.440
are we trying to comprehend today?

897
00:41:46.559 --> 00:41:48.210
Um... Loneliness.

898
00:41:48.519 --> 00:41:50.443
Hmm. Looks like
there's something in there.

899
00:41:50.559 --> 00:41:51.699
I'm going to turn it on for a minute

900
00:41:51.800 --> 00:41:52.925
and burn out the gunk.

901
00:41:53.159 --> 00:41:55.699
What did I tell you?
You'll be at Headquarters in no time.

902
00:41:55.800 --> 00:41:56.980
Whoa!

903
00:41:57.079 --> 00:41:58.206
Say, would you look at that?

904
00:41:58.639 --> 00:42:00.528
Whoa! What's happening?

905
00:42:00.679 --> 00:42:01.920
Oh, no, they turned it on.

906
00:42:02.079 --> 00:42:04.081
Huh. Never seen this before.

907
00:42:07.000 --> 00:42:10.163
My face! My beautiful face! Oh!

908
00:42:10.440 --> 00:42:12.000
- What is going on?
- We're abstracting!

909
00:42:12.079 --> 00:42:14.179
There are four stages.
This is the first:

910
00:42:14.280 --> 00:42:16.009
Non-objective Fragmentation!

911
00:42:16.119 --> 00:42:17.166
All right. Do not panic.

912
00:42:17.280 --> 00:42:20.362
What is important is that
we all stay together. Oh!

913
00:42:22.239 --> 00:42:23.650
We're in the second stage.
We're deconstructing!

914
00:42:23.960 --> 00:42:26.041
Run! Ah!

915
00:42:26.760 --> 00:42:28.250
I can't feel my legs!

916
00:42:29.000 --> 00:42:30.001
Oh, there they are.

917
00:42:30.199 --> 00:42:31.280
Come here, me!

918
00:42:33.079 --> 00:42:34.579
We've got to get out of here

919
00:42:34.679 --> 00:42:36.329
before we're nothing
but shape and color!

920
00:42:36.440 --> 00:42:38.601
Ow! We'll get stuck here forever!

921
00:42:38.840 --> 00:42:40.460
Stuck? Why did we come in here?

922
00:42:40.559 --> 00:42:42.800
I told you, it's a shortcut!

923
00:42:42.920 --> 00:42:45.047
The train!

924
00:42:48.719 --> 00:42:52.059
Oh, no. We're
two-dimensional! That's stage three!

925
00:42:52.159 --> 00:42:53.161
We're getting nowhere!

926
00:42:53.519 --> 00:42:55.840
- Depth! I'm lacking depth!
- Come on.

927
00:42:59.440 --> 00:43:00.726
We can't fit.

928
00:43:01.239 --> 00:43:03.059
Oh, no, we're Nonfigurative.

929
00:43:03.159 --> 00:43:04.730
This is the last stage!

930
00:43:04.840 --> 00:43:06.360
We're not going to make it!

931
00:43:08.599 --> 00:43:11.762
Wait! We're
two-dimensional. Fall on your face!

932
00:43:22.920 --> 00:43:24.684
Stop! Stop!

933
00:43:26.440 --> 00:43:29.250
Oh, no! I thought you said
that was a shortcut.

934
00:43:29.360 --> 00:43:32.204
I did, but wow,
we should not have gone in there.

935
00:43:32.360 --> 00:43:34.202
That was dangerous!
They really should put up a sign.

936
00:43:34.400 --> 00:43:35.599
How long until the next train?

937
00:43:35.800 --> 00:43:37.780
Who knows. But don't worry.

938
00:43:37.880 --> 00:43:39.369
There's another station. That way.

939
00:43:39.519 --> 00:43:40.885
The train always stops there.

940
00:43:41.039 --> 00:43:42.530
Right before it goes to Headquarters.

941
00:43:42.679 --> 00:43:44.409
If we hurry, we can catch it.

942
00:43:44.719 --> 00:43:46.768
This isn't another one
of your shortcuts, is it?

943
00:43:46.880 --> 00:43:48.688
Yeah!

944
00:43:49.639 --> 00:43:50.925
Is there
really another station?

945
00:43:51.039 --> 00:43:52.326
Uh-huh. Through there.

946
00:43:54.880 --> 00:43:57.166
Welcome to Imagination Land!

947
00:43:57.440 --> 00:43:58.440
Imagination Land?

948
00:43:58.559 --> 00:43:59.606
Sure!

949
00:43:59.719 --> 00:44:01.960
I come here all the time.
I'm practically the mayor.

950
00:44:02.079 --> 00:44:04.844
Hey, you guys hungry?
There's French Fry Forest!

951
00:44:04.960 --> 00:44:06.780
- Mmm! Delicious.
- No way!

952
00:44:08.039 --> 00:44:09.980
Check it out! Trophy Town!

953
00:44:10.079 --> 00:44:13.050
Medals! Ribbons! Everyone's a winner!

954
00:44:13.960 --> 00:44:15.179
I won first place!

955
00:44:15.280 --> 00:44:18.409
- Me too!
- Oh, participation award.

956
00:44:18.719 --> 00:44:21.451
Wait, is that... Sadness,
look, it's Cloud Town!

957
00:44:21.559 --> 00:44:23.219
That is my favorite!

958
00:44:23.320 --> 00:44:25.481
Oh, it's so soft!

959
00:44:25.599 --> 00:44:27.125
Oh! Let me try.

960
00:44:27.239 --> 00:44:29.128
Hey! What's the big idea?

961
00:44:29.239 --> 00:44:31.686
You better fix that wall,
or else you're in big troub...

962
00:44:34.079 --> 00:44:36.900
Oh, no! Lava! Whoo! Oh!

963
00:44:37.000 --> 00:44:38.889
Imagination Land is the best!

964
00:44:39.480 --> 00:44:42.847
Oh, is it all going
to be so interactive?

965
00:44:43.079 --> 00:44:45.219
Hey, look! The House of Cards!

966
00:44:45.320 --> 00:44:46.969
Oh, wait. Hang on just a minute.

967
00:44:47.400 --> 00:44:49.242
- Your rocket!
- Yeah.

968
00:44:49.360 --> 00:44:51.019
I stashed it in there for safekeeping,

969
00:44:51.119 --> 00:44:53.565
and now I'm all set to
take Riley to the moon!

970
00:44:54.719 --> 00:44:56.164
- Oh, I'm sorry.
- Great.

971
00:44:56.639 --> 00:44:58.688
Oh, I love Imagination Land.

972
00:44:58.840 --> 00:45:01.126
Isn't it great? And there's
always something new, like...

973
00:45:04.199 --> 00:45:05.480
Who the heck is that?

974
00:45:05.559 --> 00:45:06.721
Imaginary boyfriend.

975
00:45:07.000 --> 00:45:08.489
I would die for Riley.

976
00:45:08.679 --> 00:45:10.681
Oh, I've never seen him before.

977
00:45:10.880 --> 00:45:12.119
I live in Canada.

978
00:45:12.599 --> 00:45:14.940
Anyway, this way.
Through Preschool World!

979
00:45:15.039 --> 00:45:16.280
We're nearly to the train!

980
00:45:16.400 --> 00:45:17.599
Riley, here we come! Whoo-hoo!

981
00:45:20.440 --> 00:45:23.682
This should be fun!
New team, new friends.

982
00:45:24.079 --> 00:45:25.365
These kids look pretty good,

983
00:45:25.559 --> 00:45:27.119
considering they're from San Francisco.

984
00:45:27.199 --> 00:45:28.519
Okay, Andersen, you're up!

985
00:45:28.559 --> 00:45:30.085
- Got to go.
- Okay.

986
00:45:30.199 --> 00:45:31.440
Good luck, sweetie!

987
00:45:31.599 --> 00:45:32.681
Luck isn't going to help us now.

988
00:45:32.800 --> 00:45:34.579
If she tries to use Hockey Island,
it's going down.

989
00:45:34.679 --> 00:45:36.329
Which is why I've recalled

990
00:45:36.440 --> 00:45:38.043
every hockey memory I can think of.

991
00:45:38.320 --> 00:45:39.460
One of these has got to work

992
00:45:39.559 --> 00:45:40.980
in place of the Core Memory.

993
00:45:41.079 --> 00:45:42.411
- She's about to play!
- Hurry!

994
00:45:49.480 --> 00:45:52.449
Ha-ha! We did it, gang! It's working!

995
00:45:52.800 --> 00:45:53.800
Oh!

996
00:45:55.880 --> 00:45:57.449
Line change! Line change!

997
00:45:57.599 --> 00:45:59.409
Change it up!

998
00:46:04.360 --> 00:46:06.282
No! No! Aah!

999
00:46:11.719 --> 00:46:13.164
It's like
we don't learn anything.

1000
00:46:13.360 --> 00:46:15.300
- Come on!
- Let's pick it up out there!

1001
00:46:15.400 --> 00:46:17.019
Pass! Shoot it! Shoot it!

1002
00:46:17.119 --> 00:46:18.139
Oh!

1003
00:46:20.480 --> 00:46:21.891
- That's it!
- No, no, no! Breathe.

1004
00:46:22.000 --> 00:46:23.525
Find your happy place.

1005
00:46:26.760 --> 00:46:28.887
What's her problem?

1006
00:46:35.559 --> 00:46:37.369
- Riley. What's wrong?
- Let's go.

1007
00:46:37.559 --> 00:46:38.891
You're not going to finish tryouts?

1008
00:46:39.000 --> 00:46:40.286
- What's the point?
- Hey.

1009
00:46:40.400 --> 00:46:42.460
It'll be all right.
Let's just go back...

1010
00:46:42.559 --> 00:46:44.449
Stop saying everything
will be all right!

1011
00:46:46.679 --> 00:46:48.284
Nice hustle, ladies!

1012
00:46:56.239 --> 00:46:57.286
Hockey?

1013
00:47:00.440 --> 00:47:04.603
Oh, no, no, she loves hockey.
She can't give up hockey.

1014
00:47:04.960 --> 00:47:06.007
Hey! Look at that!

1015
00:47:06.119 --> 00:47:07.300
- Very nice shot!
- Hey!

1016
00:47:07.400 --> 00:47:09.059
Bing Bong, we have to
get to that station.

1017
00:47:09.159 --> 00:47:10.179
Sure thing. This way,

1018
00:47:10.280 --> 00:47:11.929
just past Graham Cracker Castle. Hey.

1019
00:47:12.280 --> 00:47:13.280
That's weird.

1020
00:47:13.400 --> 00:47:14.811
Graham Cracker Castle
used to be right here.

1021
00:47:14.920 --> 00:47:17.206
I wonder why
they moved it? Wow, that's not...

1022
00:47:17.360 --> 00:47:19.760
I would have sworn
Sparkle Pony Mountain was right here.

1023
00:47:19.880 --> 00:47:21.483
- Hey, what's going on?
- Yeah, yeah... I don't know...

1024
00:47:21.599 --> 00:47:23.880
- We'll have to come back.
- Princess Dream World!

1025
00:47:26.079 --> 00:47:28.731
Oh, no! The stuffed
Animal Hall of Fame!

1026
00:47:30.559 --> 00:47:31.766
My rocket!

1027
00:47:32.519 --> 00:47:34.601
Wait! Riley and I,
we're still using that rocket!

1028
00:47:34.719 --> 00:47:37.246
It still has some song power left!

1029
00:47:37.360 --> 00:47:38.960
<i>? Who's your friend who likes to play? ?</i>

1030
00:47:45.280 --> 00:47:48.940
No! No, no, no. No, you can't
take my rocket to the dump!

1031
00:47:49.039 --> 00:47:50.530
Riley and I are going to the moon!

1032
00:47:52.119 --> 00:47:53.121
Oh!

1033
00:47:56.400 --> 00:47:58.402
Riley can't be done with me.

1034
00:48:04.679 --> 00:48:08.081
Hey, it's going to be okay!
We can fix this!

1035
00:48:08.320 --> 00:48:10.083
We just need to
get back to Headquarters.

1036
00:48:10.239 --> 00:48:11.480
Which way to the train station?

1037
00:48:11.719 --> 00:48:13.960
I had a whole trip planned for us.

1038
00:48:15.000 --> 00:48:17.606
Hey, who's ticklish, huh?

1039
00:48:17.719 --> 00:48:19.802
Here comes the tickle monster!

1040
00:48:21.559 --> 00:48:22.800
Hey, Bing Bong! Look at this!

1041
00:48:26.079 --> 00:48:27.126
Oh! Here's a fun game!

1042
00:48:27.239 --> 00:48:31.210
You point to the train station
and we all go there!

1043
00:48:31.400 --> 00:48:34.528
Won't that be fun? Come on,
let's go to the train station!

1044
00:48:36.400 --> 00:48:38.128
I'm sorry they took your rocket.

1045
00:48:39.199 --> 00:48:41.009
They took something that you loved.

1046
00:48:41.880 --> 00:48:43.530
It's gone. Forever.

1047
00:48:43.800 --> 00:48:45.820
Sadness. Don't make him feel worse.

1048
00:48:45.920 --> 00:48:46.920
Sorry.

1049
00:48:47.039 --> 00:48:48.690
It's all I had left of Riley.

1050
00:48:49.400 --> 00:48:51.925
I bet you and Riley
had great adventures.

1051
00:48:52.280 --> 00:48:54.248
Oh, they were wonderful.

1052
00:48:54.400 --> 00:48:56.003
Once we flew back in time.

1053
00:48:56.159 --> 00:48:57.923
We had breakfast twice that day.

1054
00:48:58.199 --> 00:48:59.260
Sadness...

1055
00:48:59.360 --> 00:49:01.726
It sounds amazing. I bet Riley liked it.

1056
00:49:02.280 --> 00:49:05.762
Oh, she did.
We were best friends.

1057
00:49:06.800 --> 00:49:08.688
Yeah. It's sad.

1058
00:49:14.519 --> 00:49:15.521
Wh...

1059
00:49:21.360 --> 00:49:22.521
I'm okay now.

1060
00:49:24.199 --> 00:49:27.123
Come on. The train station is this way.

1061
00:49:33.719 --> 00:49:34.880
How did you do that?

1062
00:49:35.039 --> 00:49:37.088
Oh, I don't know. He was sad.

1063
00:49:37.280 --> 00:49:38.440
So I listened to what...

1064
00:49:38.559 --> 00:49:40.369
Hey! There's the train!

1065
00:49:51.519 --> 00:49:55.081
Oh! We made it!
We're finally going to get home!

1066
00:49:56.239 --> 00:49:59.641
Oh, no! These Facts and Opinions
look so similar.

1067
00:49:59.760 --> 00:50:01.922
Oh, don't worry about it.
Happens all the time.

1068
00:50:06.719 --> 00:50:07.800
On a scale of one to ten,

1069
00:50:07.920 --> 00:50:09.340
I give this day an F.

1070
00:50:09.440 --> 00:50:12.250
Well, why don't we quit standing
around and do something?

1071
00:50:12.360 --> 00:50:13.380
Like what, genius?

1072
00:50:13.480 --> 00:50:15.369
Like quitting. That's what I'm doing.

1073
00:50:15.679 --> 00:50:17.409
Sure it's the coward's way out.

1074
00:50:17.559 --> 00:50:19.527
But this coward's gonna survive.

1075
00:50:21.719 --> 00:50:22.721
Ow!

1076
00:50:27.519 --> 00:50:29.045
Emotions can't quit, genius!

1077
00:50:30.360 --> 00:50:32.931
Ugh! I thought we were supposed to
be keeping Riley happy.

1078
00:50:33.639 --> 00:50:35.085
Wait a minute! Wait a minute!

1079
00:50:36.280 --> 00:50:37.405
Mmm.

1080
00:50:38.599 --> 00:50:40.443
Aha!

1081
00:50:41.039 --> 00:50:42.280
- What is it?
- Oh, nothing.

1082
00:50:42.639 --> 00:50:44.641
- Just the best idea ever.
- What?

1083
00:50:45.000 --> 00:50:46.286
All the good Core Memories

1084
00:50:46.400 --> 00:50:47.606
were made in Minnesota.

1085
00:50:47.719 --> 00:50:50.739
Ergo, we go back to Minnesota
and make more.

1086
00:50:50.840 --> 00:50:51.887
- Ta-da!
- Wait, wait, wait.

1087
00:50:52.079 --> 00:50:53.844
You're saying we run away?

1088
00:50:54.119 --> 00:50:55.380
Well, I wouldn't call it that.

1089
00:50:55.480 --> 00:50:57.960
I'd call it the Happy Core
Memory Development program.

1090
00:50:58.239 --> 00:50:59.365
You can't be serious.

1091
00:50:59.480 --> 00:51:00.766
Hey! Our life was perfect

1092
00:51:00.960 --> 00:51:03.260
until Mom and Dad decided to move to

1093
00:51:03.360 --> 00:51:04.849
San Fran Stinktown.

1094
00:51:05.079 --> 00:51:07.161
I mean,
it's just so drastic!

1095
00:51:07.320 --> 00:51:09.447
Need I remind you
of how great things were there?

1096
00:51:09.639 --> 00:51:11.260
Our room? Our back yard?

1097
00:51:11.360 --> 00:51:12.360
Our friends?

1098
00:51:14.079 --> 00:51:15.730
<i>- ? TripleDent gum ?</i>
<i>- ? Will make you smile ?</i>

1099
00:51:15.840 --> 00:51:18.121
Did I ask for the gum commercial?

1100
00:51:18.159 --> 00:51:19.719
Anyway, it was better, that's my point.

1101
00:51:19.840 --> 00:51:22.260
Yeah, Riley was happier in Minnesota.

1102
00:51:22.360 --> 00:51:24.719
Wait. Hold on. Shouldn't we
just sleep on this or something?

1103
00:51:24.800 --> 00:51:26.300
Fine. Let's sleep on it.

1104
00:51:26.400 --> 00:51:29.324
Because, hey,
I'm sure jolly fun-filled times

1105
00:51:29.440 --> 00:51:31.329
are just around the corner.

1106
00:51:37.800 --> 00:51:38.847
Huh?

1107
00:51:43.760 --> 00:51:45.329
Hey, hey! Why aren't we moving?

1108
00:51:45.480 --> 00:51:47.686
Riley's gone to sleep.
We're all on break.

1109
00:51:48.039 --> 00:51:49.659
You mean we're
stuck here until morning?

1110
00:51:49.760 --> 00:51:51.619
Yeah, the Train of Thought
doesn't run while she's asleep.

1111
00:51:51.719 --> 00:51:53.005
Oh, we can't wait that long.

1112
00:51:53.440 --> 00:51:56.204
- How about we wake her up?
- Sadness, that's ridiculous!

1113
00:51:56.360 --> 00:51:57.929
How could we possibly...

1114
00:51:59.719 --> 00:52:00.920
How about we wake her up?

1115
00:52:01.079 --> 00:52:02.922
- Great idea, Joy.
- Thanks. Come on!

1116
00:52:08.119 --> 00:52:10.360
Whoa! This place is huge!

1117
00:52:10.599 --> 00:52:13.126
Yeah, it looks so much smaller
than I expected.

1118
00:52:13.400 --> 00:52:15.139
Wow! I Can Fly?

1119
00:52:15.239 --> 00:52:16.923
I love that one!

1120
00:52:18.039 --> 00:52:20.407
Rainbow Unicorn!
She's right there!

1121
00:52:23.559 --> 00:52:25.449
My friend says you're famous.

1122
00:52:25.559 --> 00:52:26.561
She wants your autograph.

1123
00:52:26.679 --> 00:52:29.251
No, no, Sadness,
don't bother Miss Unicorn, okay?

1124
00:52:29.400 --> 00:52:30.659
Sorry, she's from out of town.

1125
00:52:30.760 --> 00:52:32.045
That was so embarrassing, right?

1126
00:52:33.760 --> 00:52:35.762
I loved you in
Fairy Dream Adventure Part 7.

1127
00:52:35.920 --> 00:52:36.920
Okay, bye. I love you!

1128
00:52:38.960 --> 00:52:40.500
Huh. Wonder what that means.

1129
00:52:40.599 --> 00:52:41.840
Oh, well, let's go in.

1130
00:52:44.119 --> 00:52:45.769
Set up the classroom set!

1131
00:52:45.880 --> 00:52:46.980
Today's memories are in!

1132
00:52:47.079 --> 00:52:48.809
We've got
a lot to work with here.

1133
00:52:48.920 --> 00:52:50.251
Riley dumped her best friend,

1134
00:52:50.360 --> 00:52:51.804
had a miserable day at school,

1135
00:52:51.920 --> 00:52:52.920
and quit hockey.

1136
00:52:53.039 --> 00:52:55.239
The writers have
put together a killer script!

1137
00:52:55.559 --> 00:52:57.244
Just because Joy and Sadness are gone,

1138
00:52:57.400 --> 00:52:58.889
I have to do stupid Dream Duty.

1139
00:53:00.840 --> 00:53:02.659
Okay. How are we going to wake her up?

1140
00:53:02.760 --> 00:53:05.603
Well, she wakes up sometimes
when she has a scary dream.

1141
00:53:05.719 --> 00:53:07.324
- We could scare her.
- Scare her?

1142
00:53:07.440 --> 00:53:09.123
No, she's been through enough already.

1143
00:53:09.239 --> 00:53:10.699
- But, Joy...
- Sadness, you may know your way

1144
00:53:10.800 --> 00:53:12.608
around down here, but I know Riley.

1145
00:53:12.760 --> 00:53:13.965
We're gonna make her so happy,

1146
00:53:14.079 --> 00:53:16.208
she'll wake up with exhilaration.

1147
00:53:16.320 --> 00:53:17.606
We'll excite her awake!

1148
00:53:17.719 --> 00:53:19.500
That's never happened before.

1149
00:53:19.599 --> 00:53:21.500
Ooh!
Riley loves dogs. Put this on.

1150
00:53:21.599 --> 00:53:22.681
I don't think that'll work.

1151
00:53:22.800 --> 00:53:24.000
- Bing Bong?
- Yeah?

1152
00:53:24.400 --> 00:53:26.641
Don't let anything happen to these.

1153
00:53:26.800 --> 00:53:27.880
Got it.

1154
00:53:28.159 --> 00:53:30.811
Mmm-hmm. Add the reality
distortion filter.

1155
00:53:33.039 --> 00:53:35.699
Love it. Remember,
play to the camera, everyone!

1156
00:53:35.800 --> 00:53:37.130
Riley is the camera!

1157
00:53:37.239 --> 00:53:39.402
Makeup, get out of there,
we are on in five,

1158
00:53:39.519 --> 00:53:40.806
four, three...

1159
00:53:43.280 --> 00:53:44.565
Hello, class.

1160
00:53:45.320 --> 00:53:48.539
Before we begin today's pop quiz...

1161
00:53:48.639 --> 00:53:50.369
Man, she is one bad actress.

1162
00:53:50.480 --> 00:53:52.208
...which counts for 90%
of your final grade,

1163
00:53:52.920 --> 00:53:57.050
I want to introduce
our new student. Riley.

1164
00:53:57.679 --> 00:53:59.170
Would you like to stand up

1165
00:53:59.280 --> 00:54:00.644
- and introduce yourself?
- Camera.

1166
00:54:02.480 --> 00:54:04.244
And cue Riley.

1167
00:54:04.440 --> 00:54:05.980
<i>My name is Riley Andersen.</i>

1168
00:54:06.079 --> 00:54:08.923
<i>I'm from Minnesota and now I live here.</i>

1169
00:54:09.679 --> 00:54:11.443
Ew, look! Her teeth are falling out!

1170
00:54:13.440 --> 00:54:14.440
- That's disgusting.
- Ew, gross!

1171
00:54:14.599 --> 00:54:15.739
Teeth falling out.

1172
00:54:15.840 --> 00:54:17.099
Yeah, I'm used to that one.

1173
00:54:18.639 --> 00:54:20.050
Let me guess, we have no pants on.

1174
00:54:20.159 --> 00:54:22.400
Hey, look!
She came to school with no pants on!

1175
00:54:22.519 --> 00:54:24.521
- Called it!
- Ready?

1176
00:54:24.719 --> 00:54:26.688
I don't think
this happy thing is going to work.

1177
00:54:26.800 --> 00:54:27.847
But if we scare her...

1178
00:54:27.960 --> 00:54:29.449
Just follow my lead. Here we go.

1179
00:54:31.119 --> 00:54:32.849
Bark! Bark! Bark!

1180
00:54:33.400 --> 00:54:35.686
- Who is that?
- Uh, what's going on?

1181
00:54:42.159 --> 00:54:43.525
Psst! You're on! Go!

1182
00:54:44.320 --> 00:54:46.099
Whoo! Let's party!

1183
00:54:46.199 --> 00:54:47.849
Let's dance! Whoo!

1184
00:54:48.119 --> 00:54:49.201
Hey, a party.

1185
00:54:50.679 --> 00:54:51.820
Bark, bark, bark!

1186
00:54:51.920 --> 00:54:53.842
Joy, this isn't working.

1187
00:54:55.599 --> 00:54:56.619
Huh!

1188
00:54:59.920 --> 00:55:01.659
Huh? Sadness, what are you doing?

1189
00:55:01.760 --> 00:55:04.081
Come back here!

1190
00:55:04.639 --> 00:55:06.880
It's just a dream,
it's just a dream. It's just a dream.

1191
00:55:08.719 --> 00:55:11.199
They're trying to wake her up.
Call security!

1192
00:55:12.360 --> 00:55:13.804
Hi, Riley, it's me!

1193
00:55:14.280 --> 00:55:15.405
<i>- ? Who's your friend ?</i>
- Bing Bong?

1194
00:55:15.519 --> 00:55:16.780
<i>? Who likes to play?
Bing Bong, Bing Bong! ?</i>

1195
00:55:16.880 --> 00:55:18.500
Sadness, stop!
It was working!

1196
00:55:18.599 --> 00:55:19.601
Ow.

1197
00:55:20.320 --> 00:55:22.539
Sadness! You are ruining this dream!
You're scaring her!

1198
00:55:22.639 --> 00:55:23.641
But look, it's working!

1199
00:55:25.000 --> 00:55:26.000
Whoa.

1200
00:55:26.079 --> 00:55:27.809
They are not part
of this dream. Get them!

1201
00:55:28.480 --> 00:55:30.280
- Stop right there!
- Ow!

1202
00:55:31.719 --> 00:55:32.766
Pan away! Pan away!

1203
00:55:37.159 --> 00:55:39.208
Boo! Pick a plotline!

1204
00:55:39.320 --> 00:55:41.048
- Ow! Careful!
- Hold still!

1205
00:55:41.199 --> 00:55:42.405
You can't do this!

1206
00:55:42.519 --> 00:55:44.362
I know people
in Headquarters!

1207
00:55:46.760 --> 00:55:49.650
Ow! Cut that out!
Ow! Please!

1208
00:55:50.280 --> 00:55:51.769
Do you like candy? You look hungry.

1209
00:55:51.920 --> 00:55:53.922
I get you candy! Oh no!

1210
00:55:54.039 --> 00:55:55.768
No, no. No, no!

1211
00:55:55.880 --> 00:55:57.820
There go the Core Memories!

1212
00:55:57.920 --> 00:55:59.739
I can't go in there!
I'm scared of the dark!

1213
00:55:59.840 --> 00:56:00.965
Please!

1214
00:56:01.199 --> 00:56:02.280
Oh, come on.

1215
00:56:04.519 --> 00:56:05.601
What is this place?

1216
00:56:05.719 --> 00:56:06.900
The Subconscious.

1217
00:56:07.000 --> 00:56:09.001
It's where they take
all the troublemakers.

1218
00:56:14.239 --> 00:56:15.239
My hat feels loose.

1219
00:56:15.320 --> 00:56:16.481
Mmm. How do we get in?

1220
00:56:16.639 --> 00:56:17.686
Let me see.

1221
00:56:17.800 --> 00:56:19.599
You got my hat?
Or is that your hat?

1222
00:56:20.039 --> 00:56:21.019
Yeah, it's my hat.

1223
00:56:21.119 --> 00:56:23.159
You sure? I don't know,
look in the label.

1224
00:56:23.239 --> 00:56:25.460
- Yeah, it says, "My hat."
- Wait, it says, "My hat"?

1225
00:56:25.559 --> 00:56:27.324
- My hat, it says.
- That's what I wrote in my hat.

1226
00:56:27.440 --> 00:56:28.699
- What are you talking about?
- You've got my hat on.

1227
00:56:28.800 --> 00:56:30.559
Okay, but it's my handwriting.

1228
00:56:30.800 --> 00:56:32.882
- Hey! You!
- Oh! You caught us!

1229
00:56:34.079 --> 00:56:35.300
Get back in there!

1230
00:56:35.400 --> 00:56:36.889
No escaping!

1231
00:56:46.159 --> 00:56:47.300
I don't like it here.

1232
00:56:47.400 --> 00:56:49.260
It's where they keep
Riley's darkest fears.

1233
00:56:52.599 --> 00:56:54.125
It's broccoli.

1234
00:56:56.920 --> 00:56:58.360
The stairs to the basement!

1235
00:57:00.960 --> 00:57:02.485
Grandma's vacuum cleaner!

1236
00:57:11.159 --> 00:57:12.365
Okay, come on.

1237
00:57:14.199 --> 00:57:15.246
Would you walk quieter?

1238
00:57:15.360 --> 00:57:16.360
I'm trying.

1239
00:57:16.840 --> 00:57:17.840
What is going...

1240
00:57:20.039 --> 00:57:22.041
Candy wrappers?

1241
00:57:32.119 --> 00:57:34.043
- Bing Bong!
- Joy?

1242
00:57:34.360 --> 00:57:36.362
- There you are.
- Shhh!

1243
00:57:42.400 --> 00:57:43.731
It's Jangles.

1244
00:57:44.159 --> 00:57:46.079
Who's the birthday girl?
Who's the birthday girl?

1245
00:57:58.199 --> 00:57:59.440
<i>Do you have the Core Memories?</i>

1246
00:57:59.639 --> 00:58:00.925
Yeah.

1247
00:58:01.079 --> 00:58:03.081
All he cared about was the candy!

1248
00:58:04.280 --> 00:58:05.300
Shh.

1249
00:58:20.920 --> 00:58:23.161
We're out of here!
Let's get to that train!

1250
00:58:23.840 --> 00:58:26.019
Wait! The train's not running.

1251
00:58:26.119 --> 00:58:27.849
We still have to wake up Riley.

1252
00:58:27.960 --> 00:58:29.041
But how?

1253
00:58:32.159 --> 00:58:33.286
Oh, no!

1254
00:58:51.239 --> 00:58:52.340
Hey, Sadness.

1255
00:58:52.440 --> 00:58:55.780
Did you hear
about the pa-pa-party they were having?

1256
00:58:55.880 --> 00:58:57.608
Oh, yeah. Oh, yes, Joy.

1257
00:58:57.719 --> 00:59:00.326
Isn't it a birthday party?

1258
00:59:00.559 --> 00:59:01.699
Did you say

1259
00:59:01.800 --> 00:59:03.483
birthday?

1260
00:59:03.639 --> 00:59:05.539
And there's going to be
cake and presents.

1261
00:59:05.639 --> 00:59:06.800
And games and balloons...

1262
00:59:06.920 --> 00:59:08.284
A birthday?

1263
00:59:08.599 --> 00:59:10.090
Okay. Follow us!

1264
00:59:12.280 --> 00:59:14.159
Nothing like a good scare
to wake you up, right?

1265
00:59:14.400 --> 00:59:15.639
Okay, but it's my handwriting.

1266
00:59:15.800 --> 00:59:17.360
No it isn't. That's my... I wrote that.

1267
00:59:17.400 --> 00:59:18.481
No, but this one's my handwriting.

1268
00:59:37.800 --> 00:59:40.007
Who's the birthday girl?

1269
00:59:44.760 --> 00:59:46.329
- Whoo-hoo!
- Come on, let's go!

1270
00:59:53.159 --> 00:59:55.208
Ha-ha! We made it!

1271
00:59:56.119 --> 00:59:58.168
